Expected elements: present

This is a designed dark theme, not an inversion: the muted and hairline tokens swap roles between themes (#565656 is the pane rule in dark and muted text in light; #919191 is muted text in dark and the rule in light), and the surface ladder — #000000 canvas, #1B1B1B pane, #282828 pane header, #202020 chip, #565656 rule — holds across all four panes.

(a) Fade — confirmed, with one part refuted. The EXECUTIONS note's own token is #919191 = 5.47:1, only 1.2x above the floor, so the mask crosses 4.5:1 after just 12.5% opacity loss (white #F3F3F3 needs 52%). Its second line (y 874–885) sits 9px clear of the transaction pane's inner bottom — fully inside the box — and renders 4.07:1 at the ascender, 3.53→2.46:1 across the x-height, 2.10:1 at the baseline. That confirms the light lens's 2.19–2.22:1. Refuted here: no nested surface falls inside any ramp, and all four pane bottom rules render #565656 intact (2.35:1 on pane, 2.86:1 on canvas). The Code pane escapes — its last full line (51) is unfaded at 5.47/10.29:1. Values has no fade.

Glyphs, re-measured independently: ⊙ vs ⊘ IoU 0.842 (coverage-normalised, best-fit aligned), ink differs 12.6% — separated by hue alone. ⊙ and the neutral · are the identical hex #06B6D4. ⊙ on the current line has a 4.26:1 ceiling, median 2.29:1, flanks 2.10–2.67:1.

Fixes: lift the note's token or start the ramp one line-height lower; give ⊙ a filled centre.

Rating: 6/10

